---
import Layout from '../../../layouts/Layout.astro';

const photo = {
  src: '/images/oop.jpg',
  alt: 'MIPT programming lecture showing a lecturer and diagrams of linked lists and memory addresses.',
  caption: 'From a recorded lecture on data structures and memory management',
};
---

<Layout title="Object-Oriented Programming at MIPT — Nikita Ostroukhov" description="Nikita Ostroukhov’s Object-Oriented Programming course at MIPT.">
  <header><h1>Object-Oriented Programming at MIPT</h1><p class="subtitle">Designed and taught an annual programming course for second-year students. 80+ students over four years.</p></header>
  <section>
    <p>
      I became involved in teaching early in my time at MIPT, first as a mentor
      at <a href="https://miptstream.ru/2015/08/16/tehnotrek-obrazovatelnyiy-proekt-mail-ru-group-i-mfti/">TechnoTrack</a>, a joint programme by Mail.Ru Group and MIPT,
      and later teaching school students at MIPT’s Evening School. This eventually led me to teaching my own C++ and
      object-oriented programming course for second-year students.
    </p>
    <p>
      I have never been particularly fond of programming contests and tests as
      a way of learning software development. After my first year of teaching,
      I began rebuilding the course around project work instead. 
    </p>
    <p>
      During the first semester, students learned C++ by building games directly.
      In the second, they revisited the same problems by designing reusable game,
      graphics and physics engines. Code that had previously been scattered
      throughout a game could now be expressed through much smaller and clearer
      programs built on top of those abstractions.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong class="course-main-idea">The main idea of the course was one constraint</strong>: students could not use their own
      engines for the final games. Teams exchanged them. This made interfaces
      and design decisions matter to somebody other than their authors, while
      giving students experience integrating unfamiliar code and dealing with
      the practical relationship between a software developer and their users.
    </p>
    <figure>
      {photo.src ? (
        <img src={photo.src} alt={photo.alt} loading="lazy" />
      ) : (
        <div class="photo-placeholder">Photo coming soon</div>
      )}
      {photo.caption && <figcaption>{photo.caption}</figcaption>}
    </figure>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="course-materials-heading">
    <h2 id="course-materials-heading">Course materials</h2>
    <p>Selected lecture slides from the course:</p>
    <p><a href="/docs/oop-intro.pdf">Introduction to the Course ↗</a></p>
    <p><a href="/docs/oop-functions.pdf">Code Style and Functions ↗</a></p>
  </section>

  <p><a href="/">← Back to home</a></p>
</Layout>

